# Decky focus graph (new UI controls)

Full policy: MCP `bonsai.policy.get` id=`decky-ui-focus` or [packages/bonsai-mcp/knowledge/policies/decky-ui-focus.md](../../packages/bonsai-mcp/knowledge/policies/decky-ui-focus.md). Reference implementations: [focus-graph-patterns.md](../../packages/bonsai-mcp/knowledge/architecture/focus-graph-patterns.md).

- ALWAYS design new Settings/QAM rows as an **explicit focus graph in the section parent** (list each stop, wire `onMoveUp`/`onMoveDown`/`onMoveLeft`/`onMoveRight`/`onButtonDown` on the **Deck focus owner**, verify on-device). Mirror `SettingsTabUiScaleSection.tsx`, `OllamaTab.tsx`, or `PullModelsModal.tsx`.

- NEVER assume DOM order or nested `DeckFocusSlider` thumbs join the vertical graph. For sliders, ALWAYS add a document-flow **`Focusable` bridge** in the parent with vertical **and** horizontal handlers, or use proven parent ref wiring (`focusOllamaKeepAliveThumb` pattern).

- NEVER hop between Decky D-pad siblings via `document.querySelector` / aria / `data-*` / class lookup or `document.activeElement` success checks — those miss on Deck and yield wrong spatial nav. ALWAYS register mounted focus owners (refs/registry) and return `true` from `onMove*` when the target is registered (`replyStopRegistry.ts`).

- NEVER mark Deck-facing UI done without a **D-pad row in `docs/testing.md`** for the new control chain.
